content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-107 - AquaDyne HF-300 end-suction centrifugal pump, serial HF3-22950",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end vibration is 5.5 mm/s RMS. This falls in Zone C (4.5 to 7.1 mm/s RMS), 'Restricted - plan maintenance', on the HF-300 severity chart (Figure 3). It is below the 7.1 mm/s Zone D limit ('Damage likely - stop the pump'), so an immediate stop is not required. The manual says to classify the highest reading from both bearing housings and act on that zone.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C06"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Vibration has risen from 3.0 mm/s RMS last month (Zone B, 'Long-term operation') to 5.5 mm/s RMS (Zone C). That is an increase of about 83% in one month, which is a deteriorating trend.",
      "citations": [
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing housing temperature is 76 C. This is above the 70 C 'normal' limit but below the 80 C alarm and the 90 C trip. Temperature is measured on the housing surface, which matches how this reading was taken.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "No seal leakage was reported, so the 'Leakage at shaft seal' troubleshooting row does not apply at present.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing wear. It is listed as a cause of both high vibration and high bearing temperature, and both symptoms are at the drive-end housing.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment. It is also listed as a cause of both high vibration and high bearing temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Over-greasing. It can explain the high bearing temperature but is not listed as a vibration cause.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Impeller imbalance or damage. This is listed as a cause of high vibration only.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Cavitation (insufficient NPSH). This is listed as a cause of high vibration only.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Before any work, measure vibration on both bearing housings (drive end and non-drive end). Classify the highest reading using Figure 3. If any reading reaches Zone D (above 7.1 mm/s RMS), stop the pump.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Increase monitoring frequency until the repair is done. Stop the pump if the bearing housing reaches the 80 C alarm or 90 C trip, or if vibration enters Zone D.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Check the grease quantity in the bearing housings for over-greasing.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Check shaft alignment with a laser alignment tool. Tolerances: parallel offset 0.05 mm; angular 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Check NPSH or suction conditions for cavitation.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Inspect the bearings and the impeller for wear, damage or imbalance.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If either bearing shows wear, noise or high temperature, replace both bearings as a pair: DE 6312-C3 (HF3-512) and NDE 6310-C3 (HF3-510). The DE housing is currently above normal temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the back pull-out assembly is removed, isolate and drain the pump first, then remove the assembly using lifting equipment (68 kg).",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the casing is opened, fit a new casing gasket HF3-120.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the seal is disturbed, fit cartridge seal HF3-450B, not HF3-450, and tighten the gland nut to 30 Nm. Inspect the shaft sleeve and replace HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth. These rules apply because this pump's serial (HF3-22950) is covered by SB-2026-014.",
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Tighten all other fasteners to Table 5 of the manual. The Table 5 torque values are not in the evidence provided.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After any work that moves the motor or bearing housing, re-align with the laser tool to 0.05 mm parallel offset and 0.05 mm per 100 mm angular.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "On restart, confirm the seal flush (Plan 11 from pump discharge) is working and never run the pump dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After restart, confirm vibration has returned to Zone A or B (below 4.5 mm/s RMS) and housing temperature is at or below 70 C.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3 (replace as a pair with NDE bearing)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3 (replace as a pair with DE bearing)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket - replace whenever the casing is opened",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Cartridge mechanical seal - contingency, needed only if the seal is disturbed. Supersedes HF3-450 for serial HF3-22000 and above. Gland torque 30 Nm.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve - contingency, replace only if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C05"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump before opening it.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The back pull-out assembly weighs 68 kg. Lifting equipment is required.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Until repaired, stop the pump if vibration enters Zone D (above 7.1 mm/s RMS). Bearing temperature limits are 80 C alarm and 90 C trip.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The seal flush is Plan 11 from pump discharge. Never run the pump dry, including during test runs.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Bearing replacement (pair): 6.0 hours, 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: 1.5 hours, 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Contingency, if the seal must be replaced: mechanical seal replacement, 4.0 hours, 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "The seal part number conflicts between sources. The manual parts list (AQ-OM-300 Rev D) gives component seal HF3-450, while Service Bulletin SB-2026-014 (issued 14 March 2026) says not to fit HF3-450 on serial HF3-22000 and above. P-107 is serial HF3-22950, which is in that range, so the bulletin applies: use cartridge seal HF3-450B.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal gland torque also conflicts. The manual refers to Table 5, and the bulletin notes the old torque was 25 Nm. For this serial the bulletin's 30 Nm gland torque for HF3-450B applies. Table 5 and HF3-450 remain valid only for pumps below HF3-22000.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Sleeve handling differs between sources. The manual says to inspect the sleeve for scoring. The bulletin adds a replacement limit of 0.1 mm scoring depth and states that no sleeve measurement is needed for the pre-set HF3-450B. For this serial, the bulletin's criteria apply.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "What is the non-drive-end vibration reading? The manual requires both housings to be measured and the highest reading classified.",
    "What are the Table 5 fastener torque values (other than the seal gland)? They are not included in the evidence.",
    "Does bearing replacement on the HF-300 require removing the impeller or disturbing the seal? This decides whether HF3-450B, HF3-455 and the extra seal labour are needed.",
    "What grease type, quantity and relubrication interval apply? The evidence says to check grease quantity but gives no specification.",
    "What are the NPSH available and required values, used to rule out cavitation? These are not in the evidence.",
    "What are the site lockout/isolation requirements for the 400 V, 55 kW motor? These are not covered by the evidence.",
    "Do the zone limits change with time or frequency? The evidence gives no time-to-Zone-D guidance or allowed duration in Zone C, so the repair window must be set by the planner."
  ]
}
